# Tiny files

Modules stay small and single-purpose.

## Soft budgets

| Kind | Prefer | Split when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| UI component | ≤ ~100 lines | approaching ~150 or a second visual responsibility |
| Hook | ≤ ~80 lines | extracting named util functions would clarify |
| Util module | one algorithm or cohesive API | a second unrelated transform appears |
| Compound parent | layout + context + default slots | leaf markup belongs in child modules |
| Data tables | frozen constants | — data, not logic |

Typical bands: leaves ~8–25 lines; compound parents / thin hooks / compose edges ~40–70; richest leaf with a private helper, or a dense pure util, ~80–120.

## Filename = hierarchy

Use kebab names that mirror the tree:

```
file-explorer-row-name.tsx
space-wizard-share-pin-field.tsx
```

## One visual responsibility

One leaf renders one control. Name, thumb, and actions are sibling modules:

```tsx
import { Text } from '../../text/feature/text';

export function FileExplorerRowName() {
  const { file } = useFileExplorerRowContext();

  return <Text variant="label">{file.name ?? fileDefaults.name}</Text>;
}
```

## Icons

One SVG per file; named function; `WithoutStyle` SVG props (`width`, `height`, `aria-hidden` — not `className`):

```tsx
export function PinIcon(props: WithoutStyle<React.SVGProps<SVGSVGElement>>) {
  return (
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" {...props}>
      <path stroke="currentColor" d="…" />
    </svg>
  );
}
```

Place under `icons/` next to the feature that owns them.

## Private co-located helper

A private `function ThumbFallback` at the **bottom** of `file-explorer-row-thumb.tsx` fits when it is ≤ ~40 lines, presentational, and only used in that file. Shared use → its own module.

## Pure work beside UI

Row UI dispatches `reorderFiles`; list mutation lives in `util/reconcile-sort-order.ts`.

## Split cues

1. A second visual block appears → one file per block.
2. Hook accumulates named inner functions → move to `util/`.
3. Default slot JSX grows → extract compound children into modules.
4. Types/constants dominate → `util/types.ts` / `constants/` (`types-and-constants.mdc`).
